\# Source of Truth

Business documentation always overrides:

\- Existing implementation
\- AI assumptions
\- Previous conversations
\- Generated code

If documentation and code differ:

Follow the documentation.

\---

\# Before Writing Business Logic

Always verify:

✓ Business documentation has been consulted.

✓ Revenue rules are correct.

✓ User flow matches documentation.

✓ Stakeholder permissions are correct.

✓ Workflow follows documented process.

✓ Business calculations match the revenue model.

\---

\# Forbidden Practices

Never:

\- Invent business rules.
\- Modify commission calculations.
\- Skip documented workflows.
\- Change user journeys.
\- Bypass business validation.
\- Hardcode business values.
\- Ignore stakeholder responsibilities.
\- Implement undocumented business behaviour.

\---

\# Final Rule

Every business feature implemented in the GCE platform must faithfully follow the documented business model, workflows, and operational rules.

Documentation is the single source of truth.

When in doubt, read the relevant business documentation before writing code.
